  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthened institutional capacity of employers&apos; organizations</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Employers&#x2019; Consultative Association of Trinidad and Tobago (ECATT) has requested assistance from the ILO to develop a comprehensive strategic plan to guide its activities and position it for future success. This plan will address changes resulting from the Constitution amendment and the impact of the COVID-19 pandemic, focusing on institutional governance, development, resilience, and growth. The strategic plan aims to consolidate ECATT&apos;s strengths and identify opportunities to enhance its role as the leading voice of the business community through effective advocacy and lobbying efforts.

Additionally, ECATT seeks ILO support to develop a Digital Toolkit on Remote Work to assist employers in implementing or improving remote work systems tailored to their needs. This toolkit will help businesses, especially MSMEs, navigate challenges such as managing remote teams, maintaining productivity, ensuring cybersecurity, and addressing employee well-being. The ILO will also support updating ECATT&apos;s Customer Relationship Management (CRM) system and provide training to staff, enabling the Association to make data-driven decisions, inform advocacy campaigns, and encourage membership renewals, ultimately strengthening ECATT&apos;s financial and organizational capacity.</narrative>
  </description>
